title: 'save to disk: how to fork a checkpoint'
pid: 317a465f-86bc-4c5c-88be-07051e4ebe67
body: |2-
  Create your “orientation loaded” checkpoint once:

  /rename orientation-loaded

  Then whenever you want to start a new piece of work from exactly that point, while sitting in that checkpoint thread:

  /fork
  /rename whatever-this-task-is
